<%# The auditions_intro guide, shared between the auditions index and the
    first screen of the audition cycle wizard so the copy (and the user's
    dismissal) stays in one place.

    Locals:
      actions (optional) — passed through to shared/intro_guide. The wizard
                           passes none; the index offers the create CTA. %>
<%
  actions = local_assigns.fetch(:actions, [])

  auditions_guide_body = <<~HTML.html_safe
    <p>An audition cycle takes you from "we need performers" to a cast, in a few steps:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Create the sign-up form</strong> — what you want to know about each person, plus video submissions if you want them.</li>
      <li><strong>Share it</strong> — post the link anywhere; people sign up from their phone.</li>
      <li><strong>Review the responses</strong> — read submissions, watch videos, and vote with your fellow reviewers if that's your thing.</li>
      <li><strong>Assign people to audition sessions</strong> — for in-person auditions, slot everyone into scheduled sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick your cast</strong> — decide who's in, and they join your talent pool ready to be cast in shows.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>You can skip steps that don't fit — video-only cycles have no sessions, and voting is optional.</p>
  HTML
%>
<%= render "shared/intro_guide",
      guide_key: "auditions_intro",
      title: "How audition cycles work",
      body: auditions_guide_body,
      actions: actions %>
